 ],
 "literal": "As gossip rises in the town and the neighborhood makes a clamor, / the mother who has no virtue and ceaselessly harasses, / let her stay herself in her own house indeed! / While her sharp thorn-like teeth that ate gooseberries shine, / she has chosen to eat with him in the distant country, / on the slope of the mountain lying across that rose high to touch the sky, / like a garden bed where sugarcane is planted, / the water that remained in the footprint of a great male elephant.",
 "translation": "While gossip rises in the town and the neighborhood clamors, let our mother, devoid of virtue, who ceaselessly harasses us, remain alone in her house. She has gone with him to the distant country, to eat—with her sharp, thorn-like teeth that once chewed gooseberries now shining—the water that remains in the deep footprints of great bull elephants on the slopes of the high, sky-touching mountains, water that looks just like the flooded beds where sugarcane is planted.",
 "modern": "ஊரில் அலர் எழவும், சேரி மக்கள் ஆரவாரம் செய்யவும், நம்மை இடைவிடாது துன்புறுத்தும் அறமற்ற அன்னை தன் வீட்டிலேயே தனியாக இருக்கட்டும். அவள் அவரோடு தொலைதூர நாட்டிற்குச் சென்றுவிட்டாள். வானத்தைத் தொடுமளவிற்கு உயர்ந்து குறுக்கே நிற்கும் மலைச் சரிவுகளில், கரும்பு நடும் பாத்திகளைப் போலப் பெரிய ஆண் யானைகளின் காலடித் தடங்களில் தேங்கியிருக்கும் நீரை, நெல்லிக்காயைத் தின்ற அவளுடைய கூர்மையான பற்கள் மின்னும்படி அவரோடு சேர்ந்து பருகுவதையே அவள் தேர்ந்தெடுத்துவிட்டாள்.",
 "explanation": "In this poem of the Pālai landscape, the friend of the heroine speaks with a mixture of relief and concern after the heroine has eloped with her lover. She wishes that the harsh, unyielding mother who kept them under constant surveillance would remain confined to her own house. Meanwhile, the heroine has chosen to brave the difficult desert path with her lover. The image of the elephant's footprint holding water like a sugarcane bed highlights the scarcity of water in the wasteland, where even a small puddle is precious. The mention of eating gooseberries, which makes subsequent water taste sweet, symbolizes how their mutual love sweetens even the harshest circumstances of their journey.",
